 "summary": {
  "text": "Members are marking the 25th anniversary of 9/11. Volume was minimal early — one post each from @RepJoshG (Pentagon Memorial wreath, 9/2) and @RepJerryNadler (9/3), two from @Mike_CA05 on a local service (9/6), nothing on 9/7 — then @RepDanGoldman and @RepGregoryMeeks on 9/8, and seven posts from six members on 9/9. @RepJerryNadler leads on volume and drove the shift: from personal remembrance and shared \"25 years\"/\"first responders\" language toward a pointed demand that Mayor Mamdani attend the memorial, an argument @RepGregoryMeeks also made — so far just two New York members. Press on 9/8–9/9 surfaced the post-attack air-quality and dust story; no member has touched it. Whether either line spreads is open.",
